{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":68889,"duration_api_ms":68851,"num_turns":12,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c76bb8c8-debb-4f9d-8397-26b3c06d3ab6","total_cost_usd":0.370092,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31240,"cache_read_input_tokens":200814,"output_tokens":2976,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31240,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":7,"outputTokens":2976,"cacheReadInputTokens":200814,"cacheCreationInputTokens":31240,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.370092,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Independently verified all 6 amendments against the source code. 5 are confirmed real defects: the molt_cycle mixed-outcome boolean/accumulator inconsistency (fr-2-da64408d), the legacy migration firing on fresh states causing immediate juvenile molts (fr-2-61c597e4), the boolean-based accumulator undercounting multi-stage failures (fr-2-1595155b), the hardcoded detritus consumption magic constant (fr-2-c7322f22), and the 5 dead TOML preset knobs silently dropped by deserialization (fr-2-0b9a822f). The substrate porosity amendment (fr-2-ba1e4ade) is a modeling fidelity enhancement, not a correctness bug.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-2-da64408d","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified at shrimp.rs lines 510-520. When both any_failed and any_succeeded are true on a mixed-outcome day: last_molt_success is set to false (line 512), then failed_molt_accum increases by 0.3 (line 513) and decreases by 0.35 (line 519), netting -0.05. The boolean declares failure while the accumulator shows improvement. Since last_molt_success directly gates sub-adult maturation at line 863, a juvenile molt failure concurrent with an adult molt success blocks sub-adult progression despite the accumulator improving. This is a genuine state inconsistency with downstream behavioral consequences."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-ba1e4ade","decision":"reject","rationale":"The function at lines 133-140 uses the first non-trivial layer's porosity as a surface-dominated diffusion approximation. While the amendment correctly identifies reduced accuracy for thin sand caps over aquasoil, this is a deliberate modeling simplification, not an error. The current approach is physically defensible — oxygen diffusion is dominated by the surface layer in most aquarium substrates. The proposed layer-by-layer iterative Bouldin approach is a significant algorithmic enhancement to improve model fidelity, not a bug fix. The existing behavior produces reasonable (if imprecise) results for the intended use case."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-c7322f22","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified at substrate.rs line 188-191: the detritus daily consumption fraction 0.01 is hardcoded directly in the arithmetic expression. In contrast, the periphyton consumption fraction reads from process_params.microfauna_periphyton_consumption (lines 151-153). This asymmetry means one consumption pathway is tunable via configuration while the other is silently fixed. Extracting to a named constant with documentation is a minimal, low-risk improvement that makes the value discoverable and prevents it from being overlooked during parameter tuning."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-61c597e4","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified across three locations. AnimalState::default() sets inter_molt_timer_days=14.0 (biology.rs:615). StageCohort::default() sets molt_timer_days=0.0 (biology.rs:112). The migration guard at shrimp.rs:410-419 fires when inter_molt_timer_days > 0 AND all three stage timers are 0 — which is exactly the default fresh state. This copies 14.0 into all stage timers. With juvenile_molt_interval_days=14.0, timer_factor = 14/14 = 1.0, triggering immediate molt on the first tick. The migration was intended for old save files but its guard condition cannot distinguish fresh states from legacy states. This is a clear initialization bug."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-1595155b","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified at shrimp.rs lines 451-453 (boolean declarations) and 510-520 (accumulator logic). The any_failed/any_succeeded booleans collapse all per-stage outcomes into single +0.3/-0.35 adjustments regardless of how many stages resolved. With intervals 14/21/28, LCM overlaps at day 42 guarantee multi-stage resolution days. Two simultaneous failures add only +0.3 instead of +0.6, and a mixed day (failure + success) nets -0.05. Mortality pressure is inversely correlated with the number of simultaneous molts — the opposite of what's biologically expected. This is distinct from fr-2-da64408d (which addresses the boolean/accumulator inconsistency) and warrants independent fixing."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-0b9a822f","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified across all files. The TOML (lines 23-27) defines ca_min_mg_per_l, mg_min_mg_per_l, juvenile_molt_interval_days, sub_adult_molt_interval_days, and molt_success_threshold. ShrimpPreset (presets.rs:430-478) has no corresponding fields for any of these five. Without #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)], deserialization silently drops them. While ShrimpRuntimeParams defaults (biology.rs:719-737) happen to match the TOML values exactly (20.0, 5.0, 14.0, 21.0, 0.55), the configuration is dead: editing these TOML values has zero effect. This is a maintenance trap — anyone tuning the preset file would reasonably expect these values to be applied."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"39d9100a-aeab-4a79-9a40-6e4dd6931762"}
